    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389-a5">

                <pb facs="0564" n="468" xml:id="pg468"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States at Canton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1898-03-15"><hi rendition="#italic">March 15,
                                1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">The <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York Condensed Milk
                        Company</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">71 Murray street. New York, N. Y.,
                        U. S. A.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: This district is cursed with
                    thousands of cans of condensed milk made in Germany and Japan, purporting to be
                    genuine “Gail Borden, Eagle Brand.”</p>
                <p>I have obtained by personal purchase from dealers several cans of this spurious
                    milk and shall send samples of it on to you by the next steamer, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Rio</hi>, leaving Hong-kong March 23, instant.</p>
                <p>I have also counterfeit labels, a specimen of one of which I inclose
                    herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward Bedloe</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
